Rewritten for Nodecode: the provider profile (id, display name, base URL, key
variable, signup page, the fallback route list, the chat lane), its catalog
filter (only the routes whose capabilities or supported_parameters advertise
tool calls), its catalog rates (input_per_1m / output_per_1m, carried in the
Nodecode catalog entry so a round on a priced route is costed by Nodecode
itself), its session_id, its routing preferences (only, ignore, order, sort,
allow_fallbacks, max_price), its reasoning passthrough as AnyRouter's own
`reasoning' object, and its opt-in app-attribution headers, which here name
Nodecode. The live catalog read from GET /v1/models is the /anyrouter command,
read on demand and put into /models rather than fetched at load, and the
catalog is not cached across API keys: the command's list is the one last
read. Left out: the original's in-memory per-key catalog cache with its
background audience, its cost hook in Hermes' dashboard shape (Nodecode's
catalog prices a round from the same rates), its introspection of an older
Hermes ProviderProfile's fields, and its optional ANYROUTER_BASE_URL and
ANYROUTER_APP_ATTRIBUTION environment variables, which are the `base_url' and
`attribution' members of the section here. The original's default reasoning
object for a reasoning model the caller configured nothing for
({"enabled": true, "effort": "medium"}) is not forced: an operator who chose
no effort leaves the model its own default.
